<%# The Ranked view: the spot queue in the order it will be worked.

    Two sections, because the two halves answer different questions. A PRIORITY
    session has no rank to compare — it starts whenever it is ready — so it sits
    above the queue with one button: demote it, which lands it at the head of the
    spot queue. A SPOT session has a place in line, so its row carries an editable
    precedence and a drag handle.

    Rows rather than cards: a queue is read down a column, and forty cards in a
    responsive grid have no readable "next".

    Locals:
      priority_sessions - priority sessions matching the filters, ranked
      spot_sessions     - spot sessions matching the filters, ranked
      section_limit     - how many rows each section renders at most
      status_filter     - the statuses this page is showing ([] means all)
      priority_class_filter - "spot", "priority", or nil for both
      visibility_filter - which board this is: "on_board" (the default, which
                          leaves snoozed and hidden rows out), "off_board", or
                          "all". Presentation only.
      live_insert       - false when a filter the client cannot evaluate (search,
                          agent root, genesis) is narrowing the page %>
<%# A queue that goes stale is a queue you cannot trust, so the rows subscribe to
    their own stream. Two kinds of message arrive on it.

    A status change replaces ONE element per row — the status pill — and nothing
    else. That is what keeps a live update from fighting the two interactions on
    this screen: it cannot clobber a precedence the user is halfway through
    typing, and it cannot renumber or re-seat a row mid-drag, because it never
    touches the input, the handle, or the row's position.

    A membership change ships an ENVELOPE instead (`_ranked_delivery`), because
    whether a row belongs on your screen depends on filters only your page knows.
    One stream serves every open page, so the server ships the session's
    filterable facts plus the row rendered inside an inert <template>, and
    `ranked-queue#deliveryTargetConnected` decides: insert it in precedence order,
    move it between the sections, take it away, or ignore it. That is how a
    newly-created session appears in the right section without a reload, and how a
    trashed one leaves a page filtered to live work while STAYING on a page whose
    operator ticked "Archived" specifically to look at the trash.

    Three things keep that safe. Deliveries are held while SortableJS has a row in
    hand and flushed on drop, so nothing is inserted under a moving pointer. A row
    holding focus or a dirty field is never moved or removed, the same rule the
    reconnect backfill uses. And an arriving delivery never writes another row's
    precedence input — it only ever adds, moves or removes whole rows.

    What it still deliberately does NOT do: re-sort the queue when someone else
    changes a precedence, or insert a row on a page narrowed by a search, an agent
    root or a genesis — the client cannot evaluate those three, so it declines
    rather than guessing (`live_insert`).

    Neither gap is permanent, because both lists are also
    `data-live-region="sync"`. A page whose socket died — every reopen of the iOS
    PWA — is reconciled against a fresh render on reconnect, which recovers the
    order, the grouping and any row the stream never delivered. `syncChildren`
    skips a row holding focus or a dirty field, so that reconnect cannot eat a
    precedence someone is halfway through typing either. %>
<%= turbo_stream_from Session::RANKED_STREAM %>
<section class="mb-8"
         id="ranked_sessions"
         data-controller="ranked-queue"
         data-ranked-queue-slot-gap-value="<%= SessionPrecedence::SLOT_GAP %>"
         data-ranked-queue-section-limit-value="<%= section_limit %>"
         data-ranked-queue-status-filter-value="<%= status_filter.to_json %>"
         data-ranked-queue-priority-class-filter-value="<%= priority_class_filter %>"
         data-ranked-queue-visibility-filter-value="<%= visibility_filter %>"
         data-ranked-queue-live-insert-value="<%= live_insert %>">
  <div class="mb-4">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800">Ranked</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
      Spot sessions start highest-precedence first. Drag a row to move it, or type a number and press Enter.
      Precedence is an absolute scale — 100000 comes before 50.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%# ---- Priority ---- %>
  <div class="mb-6">
    <div class="mb-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700">Priority</h3>
      <span class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 text-xs font-medium px-2 py-0.5"
            data-ranked-queue-target="priorityCount"><%= priority_sessions.size %></span>
      <span class="min-w-0 text-xs text-gray-400">start whenever they are ready — precedence does not gate them</span>
    </div>
    <%# Both lists are ALWAYS in the DOM, hidden when empty. They are Stimulus
        targets, and a target that disappears when a section empties would fail the
        controller's connect() — taking drag-and-drop and inline editing down on the
        other section with it. It is also what lets a promote/demote move a row into
        a section the server rendered empty. %>
    <ul id="ranked_priority_list" data-live-region="sync"
        class="divide-y divide-gray-100 rounded-md border border-gray-200 bg-white <%= "hidden" if priority_sessions.empty? %>"
        data-ranked-queue-target="priorityList">
      <% priority_sessions.each do |session| %>
        <%= render "sessions/ranked_row", agent_session: session, draggable_row: false %>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 rounded-md border border-dashed border-gray-200 px-3 py-4 <%= "hidden" if priority_sessions.any? %>"
       data-ranked-queue-target="priorityEmpty">No priority sessions match these filters.</p>
    <% if priority_sessions.size >= section_limit %>
      <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-gray-400">Showing the first <%= section_limit %>. Narrow the filters to see the rest.</p>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%# ---- Spot ---- %>
  <div>
    <div class="mb-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700">Spot queue</h3>
      <span class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 text-xs font-medium px-2 py-0.5"
            data-ranked-queue-target="spotCount"><%= spot_sessions.size %></span>
      <span class="min-w-0 text-xs text-gray-400">highest precedence is worked first</span>
    </div>
    <ul id="ranked_spot_list" data-live-region="sync"
        class="divide-y divide-gray-100 rounded-md border border-gray-200 bg-white <%= "hidden" if spot_sessions.empty? %>"
        data-ranked-queue-target="spotList">
      <% spot_sessions.each do |session| %>
        <%= render "sessions/ranked_row", agent_session: session, draggable_row: true %>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 rounded-md border border-dashed border-gray-200 px-3 py-4 <%= "hidden" if spot_sessions.any? %>"
       data-ranked-queue-target="spotEmpty">No spot sessions match these filters.</p>
    <% if spot_sessions.size >= section_limit %>
      <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-gray-400">Showing the first <%= section_limit %>. Narrow the filters to see the rest.</p>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%# One live region for the whole view, so a failed write says so without a
      page reload swallowing the drag the user just made. %>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-red-600 hidden" role="alert" data-ranked-queue-target="error"></p>

  <%# Where membership deliveries land. Outside both lists on purpose: it is not a
      `data-live-region`, so the reconnect backfill neither reconciles it nor
      counts its children as rows, and the lists' MutationObserver does not see a
      delivery as a row arriving. Each envelope is consumed and removed the moment
      it connects, so this stays empty between messages. %>
  <div id="ranked_deliveries" hidden></div>
</section>
